Subject: Adapt the pinned V8 C interface to sized argument and import vectors

Base: V8 245ce17ed8483e6bc3de7f668635f46c5bfdd8a0 (rusty_v8 0.106.0).
Header: WebAssembly/wasm-c-api 9d6b93764ac96cdd9db51081c363e09d2d488b4d.

The header update below is the unmodified upstream header at that revision.
The internal C++ API remains unchanged. C callbacks retain their function arities
and receive borrowed descriptors; neither the descriptor nor its storage may be
freed/replaced by the callback. Instance imports are borrowed for instantiation.
Calls reject wrong vector lengths before entering the old array-based code.

Const-correct copy signatures follow the header. The now-const source also exposes
an upstream wasm_val_vec_copy argument-order bug; copy into the temporary, not
into the input vector. A numeric vector-copy regression covers this path.
Start-function traps are returned to the embedder without printing an uncaught
exception, following V8 WasmEngine::AsyncInstantiate's silent TryCatch pattern.
The smoke test checks this in a subprocess so native output is observable.
Windows archives carry their ETW library dependency as the rusty_v8 adapter does.
The wee8 object omits default CRT directives, as rusty_v8 does, so the consumer
chooses its CRT. The native producer builds the wee8 target directly.
Like rusty_v8, wee8 explicitly depends on build/config:shared_library_deps.
This includes the configured target libc++/libc++abi objects in the complete
archive. A static-library target does not acquire that dependency automatically;
without it, consumers cannot resolve Chromium's std::__Cr symbols by linking
their system C++ library. Host-tool libc++ dependencies do not fill that gap.

This is a core-interface MVP, not full implementation of every header declaration:
tag APIs are completed/extended separately by wasm-exceptions.patch; WasmGC
values crossing the host boundary remain unsupported.
Review/remove this adapter on a V8 upgrade that implements the same header ABI.

